{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131701-effigy-of-sin-and-the-black-spiral","id":1131701,"title":"Effigy of Sin and the Black Spiral?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-20T07:39:01-07:00","id":1131701,"title":"Effigy of Sin and the Black Spiral?","content":"Mummy has a Level 8 power called Effigy of Sin where a Mummy can basically absorb sins you committed and die, thus destroying the guilt of the sins. Could such a power conceivably fix a BSD or would something deeper be required to restore one who has danced the Black Spiral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:08:07-07:00","id":1131717,"title":"","content":"Probably not fix one, but it could put them on the right path. Most BSD have committed multiple sins, and given the difficulty of that roll I doubt they could take them all. If the Mummy was to absorb the sin of dancing the spiral however, it would free the Garou to realize everything else they have done wrong. They would have the right mind to leave the tribe, seek out Erebus, and eventually they may be able to rejoin Gaian society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:08:20-07:00","id":1132259,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would be that easy. Having committed sins is different from being committed to sin willfully. Dancing the Black Spiral turns a Garou into a creature that loves evil for its own sake, and unless the mummy power removes the love of and desire to do evil, it's not going to remove the essential corruption that makes the werewolf a follower of the Wyrm -- he'll just mar his newly cleaned slate the first chance he gets. So in short, I think it would take something deeper to redeem him, though maybe it would have an effect on his apparent wyrm-taintedness in the short term?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}